{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1363725-tc-a-cultural-inspiration","id":1363725,"title":"TC:A Cultural Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-27T19:44:18-08:00","id":1363725,"title":"TC:A Cultural Inspiration","content":"Hi! Longtime Trinity fan, just starting a new campaign with the new rules, and I'm stoked!! (a terrorist plot involving rogue QK's armed with Huang-Marr Devices threatening the Kenya sky-hook, if you're interested). <br /> <br /> What I'm wondering is: what does Muzzein Bang *sound* like? What Afro-futurist inspirations can be found out there? I would love a soundtrack to my campaign that evokes these kinds of themes - are there any particular Artists or works that you would recommend to evoke future Africa? <br /> Besides music, I've obviously watched the sh*t out of Black Panther - what else is out there for a some-what out of touch (but learning!) 30-something? <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T00:16:45-08:00","id":1363749,"title":"","content":"Please remember that all of the Trinity Continuum game lines begin with A -- \u00c6on, Aberrant, Adventure!, Assassins -- so &quot;TC: A&quot; doesn't do a lot to narrow down the game line you're referring to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T15:59:55-08:00","id":1363865,"title":"","content":"TC: Aeon. Thank you for pointing that out, gracious Manager - love your work!<br /> <br /> So....suggestions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T16:14:21-08:00","id":1363866,"title":"","content":"I've wondered about Bang music this myself since 1E. The description sounds sort of like electronica that heavily samples sounds from the natural world (there was a reference in 1E to a new track using a sample of Chromatic breathing woven into the rythm), that also uses a lot of old world and tribal influences. There's a Native American electronica group called &quot;A Tribe Called Red,&quot; maybe something like that, but with more sampling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T16:28:16-08:00","id":1363870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritoninvestigator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1363725-tc-a-cultural-inspiration#post1363725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! Longtime Trinity fan, just starting a new campaign with the new rules, and I'm stoked!! (a terrorist plot involving rogue QK's armed with Huang-Marr Devices threatening the Kenya sky-hook, if you're interested).<br /> <br /> What I'm wondering is: what does Muzzein Bang *sound* like? What Afro-futurist inspirations can be found out there? I would love a soundtrack to my campaign that evokes these kinds of themes - are there any particular Artists or works that you would recommend to evoke future Africa?<br /> Besides music, I've obviously watched the sh*t out of Black Panther - what else is out there for a some-what out of touch (but learning!) 30-something?<br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, instead of Afro-futurism you could go with something that would kill all interest in it: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H-YCZr0epts\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H-YCZr0epts</a><br /> <br /> Figure nothing's better for that than &quot;White African Space Jesus.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T18:58:05-08:00","id":1363891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1363725-tc-a-cultural-inspiration?p=1363866#post1363866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've wondered about Bang music this myself since 1E. The description sounds sort of like electronica that heavily samples sounds from the natural world (there was a reference in 1E to a new track using a sample of Chromatic breathing woven into the rythm), that also uses a lot of old world and tribal influences. There's a Native American electronica group called &quot;A Tribe Called Red,&quot; maybe something like that, but with more sampling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Enigma and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LKUxE8UE7S0\" target=\"_blank\">Delerium</a> often incorporate a lot of things like tribal chanting and instruments as well as Gregorian chants into layered electronic music, so that's often what I had in mind when I thought about Muzzein Bang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T19:23:08-08:00","id":1364903,"title":"","content":"From a more old school perspective, people like Sun Ra, Afrika Bambaataa, Tricky, and A Guy Called Gerald.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T21:54:12-08:00","id":1364940,"title":"","content":"A Tribe called Red is Canadian, I'm Canadian - should have been near the top of my list lol. <br /> <br /> Nice! These are all great suggestions! Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T08:32:07-08:00","id":1365014,"title":"","content":"Another possible source to check out is South African musician Johnny Clegg and his two bands, Juluka and Savuka, which combined Zulu music with Celtic, rock, and other styles. (Clegg was white, and the formation of an interracial band playing African fusion music in 1979 South Africa was pretty revolutionary. Sadly, he died last year.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}